From 903155b6b203b2a8c1eae56d36e65b553ff930ba Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 18:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] drm/amd/display: HDMI 3D: vblank timestamps of a frame packed
 mode

The doubled timing of frame packing lived only in the copy of the mode
that create_stream_for_sink() works on. The adjusted mode of the CRTC
state kept the timing of the 2D twin, and the vblank code takes its
numbers from the adjusted mode
(drm_atomic_helper_calc_timestamping_constants(), and with them
drm_crtc_vblank_helper_get_vblank_timestamp()): half the real pixel
clock and half the real line count, against scanout positions that the
hardware gives in real lines. The frame duration came out right, because
the two halves cancel. The line duration came out twice too long, and
the last lines of the frame were taken for the end of the blanking, so
the step from a scanout position to the start of the frame was wrong:
about 0.7 ms at 1080p24 for a timestamp taken at the start of the
blanking (45 lines of 18.5 us before the next frame, counted as 41 lines
of 37 us).

dm_update_crtc_state() now gives the adjusted mode of a frame packed
mode the doubled timing when it builds the stream. Nothing else in
amdgpu reads the crtc_ fields of the adjusted mode: the encoder check
reads its clock and its size, for eDP, LVDS and MST.

crtc->hwmode and amdgpu_crtc->hw_mode stay copies of the mode as user
space gave it. With the display core the first only stands in for the
blanking positions when the hardware reports none, and it reports them
whenever a stream is on; the second feeds an estimate of the power
management of old GPUs, which reads the undoubled clock in any case.

Checked: compiled with the configuration and the compiler of the image;
the figures above, by reading drm_vblank.c and
amdgpu_display_get_crtc_scanoutpos(). Not run on hardware.
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/amdgpu_dm/amdgpu_dm.c | 10 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/amdgpu_dm/amdgpu_dm.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/amdgpu_dm/amdgpu_dm.c
index 19ffb91..9173b70 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/amdgpu_dm/amdgpu_dm.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/amdgpu_dm/amdgpu_dm.c
@@ -12818,6 +12818,16 @@ static int dm_update_crtc_state(struct amdgpu_display_manager *dm,
 				goto fail;
 		}
 
+		/*
+		 * Vblank timestamps are computed from the adjusted mode
+		 * (drm_atomic_helper_calc_timestamping_constants()): give it what a frame
+		 * packed stream scans out, twice the lines at twice the clock.
+		 */
+		if (amdgpu_dm_stereo_layout(connector, &new_crtc_state->mode) ==
+		    DRM_MODE_FLAG_3D_FRAME_PACKING)
+			drm_mode_set_crtcinfo(&new_crtc_state->adjusted_mode,
+					      CRTC_STEREO_DOUBLE);
+
 		/*
 		 * If we already removed the old stream from the context
 		 * (and set the new stream to NULL) then we can't reuse
